MICHAELSON:	Things were different when you got to Io, weren't they? The relics were different, Shaw was different... your enemy was different.

ROBERTS:	Shaw seemed... off, yeah. I can't quite explain it, but... well, we all knew we had to get those relics before the Soviets did, but it seemed more important to Shaw, somehow. Like it was personal - more personal, I mean.

MICHAELSON:	How do you mean, "more personal"?

ROBERTS:	We all knew that whatever the Soviets were planning, it couldn't be good. Alien weapons technology, Supertanks, advanced fighters - and now this, whatever "this" was? We all wanted them stopped. It was personal for all of us. Shaw just seemed like he wanted it more.

MICHAELSON:	Did that... concern you, in any way?

ROBERTS:	Like I said, we all wanted it stopped and we all had our own personal reasons for wanting it - our friends next to us, people back home... Shaw is my commanding officer, and he wanted the same thing the rest of us did.
